//Problem Statement: Employee Salary Calculation Using COBOL Paragraphs
//Objective: To divide a COBOL program into separate paragraphs and execute them using the PERFORM statement for better program structure and reusability.
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. EMP-SALARY.

DATA DIVISION.
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.

01 WS-BASIC-SALARY PIC 9(5).
01 WS-ALLOWANCE    PIC 9(5).
01 WS-TOTAL-SALARY PIC 9(6).

PROCEDURE DIVISION.

    PERFORM ACCEPT-DATA
    PERFORM CALCULATE-SALARY
    PERFORM DISPLAY-RESULT

    STOP RUN.

ACCEPT-DATA.

    DISPLAY "ENTER BASIC SALARY:"
    ACCEPT WS-BASIC-SALARY

    DISPLAY "ENTER ALLOWANCE:"
    ACCEPT WS-ALLOWANCE.

CALCULATE-SALARY.

    COMPUTE WS-TOTAL-SALARY =
        WS-BASIC-SALARY + WS-ALLOWANCE.

DISPLAY-RESULT.

    DISPLAY "TOTAL SALARY: " WS-TOTAL-SALARY.
